AutoDock CUDA-MP
Experimental CUDA-accelerated implementation of AutoDock focused on exploring GPU parallelism for molecular docking and binding-energy evaluation.
This repository contains a modified AutoDock codebase with CUDA-specific components designed to move computationally intensive portions of the docking workflow to NVIDIA GPUs.
Note
This is an experimental/research project based on AutoDock. It is not the official AutoDock distribution.

Overview
Molecular docking attempts to predict how a small molecule — such as a ligand or drug candidate — binds to a receptor with a known three-dimensional structure.
Docking algorithms can require a large number of energy evaluations while exploring possible ligand conformations. These calculations make molecular docking an interesting target for parallel computing.
AutoDock CUDA-MP explores the use of NVIDIA CUDA to accelerate parts of this workload.
The project combines the existing AutoDock C/C++ codebase with CUDA kernels and GPU-oriented data preparation.
Goals
The main goals of this project are:
- Explore GPU acceleration of AutoDock workloads.
- Parallelize computationally expensive energy evaluations.
- Experiment with CUDA-based molecular docking.
- Reduce execution time for compute-intensive docking workloads.
- Investigate heterogeneous CPU/GPU execution for scientific computing.
Architecture
At a high level, the project follows the traditional AutoDock workflow while introducing CUDA-based execution for selected computational stages.
                 AutoDock
                    |
                    v
          Ligand / receptor data
                    |
                    v
             Grid preparation
                    |
                    v
          Search / conformations
                    |
                    v
        +----------------------+
        |   Energy Evaluation  |
        +----------+-----------+
                   |
             CUDA execution
                   |
                   v
        +----------------------+
        |     NVIDIA GPU       |
        |                      |
        |  Parallel evaluation |
        |  of docking states   |
        +----------+-----------+
                   |
                   v
            Docking results
CUDA-related components in the repository include files such as:
eval_wrapper.cu
cuda_wrapper.h
eAllocPrepCuda.cc
eMapPrepCuda.cc
eMapPrepCuda.h
These components provide the bridge between the existing AutoDock implementation and GPU execution.
Technology
The project primarily uses:
- C
- C++
- NVIDIA CUDA
- GNU Autotools
- Make
- AutoDock 4 codebase
Requirements
To build the CUDA-enabled version you will need a development environment containing:
- C/C++ compiler
- GNU Make
- Autoconf / Automake
- NVIDIA GPU
- NVIDIA CUDA Toolkit
- Compatible NVIDIA driver
Verify that CUDA is available:
nvcc --version
Verify that the GPU is visible:
nvidia-smi
Building
Clone the repository:
git clone https://github.com/evertonmj/autodock-cudamp.git
cd autodock-cudamp
If configure.ac has been modified, regenerate the configuration files:
aclocal
autoconf
Configure the project with CUDA support:
./configure --prefix=/path/to/install --enable-cuda
If the project was previously configured without CUDA support, clean the previous build:
make clean
Compile:
make
Install:
make install
The resulting AutoDock executable should be available under:
/path/to/install/bin
CUDA Build
CUDA support is enabled during configuration:
./configure --enable-cuda
Or, when installing without root privileges:
./configure \
    --prefix=$HOME/autodock-cuda \
    --enable-cuda

make
make install
The configuration process enables the CUDA-specific sections of the source code used during compilation.
